  <p>
    The General Aptitude Test is a CUET section that DU describes as covering general knowledge, current affairs, mental ability, numerical ability, quantitative reasoning (basic arithmetic, algebra, geometry, mensuration and statistics) and logical reasoning. It is school-level, but it is not nothing.
  </p>

