  <h2 id="read-line">How to read any university's CUET line in three steps</h2>

  <p>
    Delhi University is one of 244 universities that used CUET scores in 2026. The same three steps work for any of them.
  </p>

  <ol class="rich-list">
    <li><strong>Find the programme-specific line.</strong> Open the university's own admission notice and search for your programme. Skip coaching summaries, since they copy last year's rules.</li>
    <li><strong>Check each subject against your marksheet.</strong> If a line asks for Mathematics and you did not study it, that line is closed for you, even if the rest of the combination fits.</li>
    <li><strong>Check for extra sections.</strong> A General Aptitude Test or a university test adds a quant section you can practise, so note it in your plan.</li>
  </ol>

