  <h2 id="pro">CA, CS and CMA: timing, not eligibility</h2>

  <p>
    Eligibility for these three is the easy part, and the sibling guide covers it. In this cycle the real question is timing, because each has its own sitting calendar and registration rule.
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li><strong>CA Foundation:</strong> you must register at least four months before the exam. The January 2027 window closed on 1 September 2026. For the May 2027 sitting, the reported last date is 1 January 2027.</li>
    <li><strong>CMA Foundation:</strong> the December 2026 exam is reported for 13 December, with a registration deadline of 10 October and a late-fee window to 17 October. That is five days after 5 October 2026.</li>
    <li><strong>CSEET (CS entry):</strong> ICSI's February 2027 session has conflicting registration dates in public sources, so confirm on icsi.edu before you rely on either.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="highlight-box highlight-box--amber">
    <p>
      <strong>Multi-stage competition:</strong> these are entry gates, not finish lines. Each is followed by harder stages and, for CA, articleship.
    </p>
    <p>
      Reported CA Foundation pass rates in the last three sittings were about 14.8%, 19.2% and 20.1%. The sittings do not report results by maths background, so the numbers say nothing about no-maths students.
    </p>
  </div>

  <p>
    The collision to watch is May 2027. CUET is expected from the second week of May, IPMAT in early May, and a CA Foundation sitting runs that month.
  </p>

  <p>
    You cannot give all three your best. If CUET and a DU seat are your base, treat CA Foundation as a later sitting rather than May, since ICAI has recently held Foundation in September, January and May.
  </p>

  <p>
    If you are weighing the credentials against each other, <a href="/blog/career-options/ca-vs-cma-vs-cfa-india-which-is-better/">CA vs CMA vs CFA</a> compares them, and <a href="/blog/career-options/career-after-bcom-other-than-ca-and-mba/">careers after BCom other than CA and MBA</a> maps the alternatives.
  </p>

